\paragraph{Temperature controls degeneracy and LP spread.}
Table~\ref{tab:t_degeneracy} reports instance degeneracy (constant F1, gold-filtered) and median within-instance LP range across four temperatures on a separate SciERC ablation run.
Both quantities are strictly monotonic in $T$: degeneracy falls from 32.8\% ($T{=}0.5$) to 8.0\% ($T{=}1.2$), while LP range increases from 0.022 to 0.075 nats.
Temperature thus provides a direct lever for practitioners to shift the degeneracy regime; however, because LP-quality alignment is model-intrinsic (\S\ref{sec:fewnerd}), reducing degeneracy alone may not suffice for selection gains.

